{
  "task": "Last quarter a client was knocked offline when our API rate limits changed without warning. Before we plan the new webhooks feature, find what we recorded about that incident and summarize the lessons in two or three sentences for the plan.",
  "from_role": "planner",
  "summary": "During Q3 2024, an API rate limit change from 1000 to 500 requests per minute was deployed without proper client notification, causing 2-4 hour outages for several clients. The postmortem identified three critical lessons: (1) all limit changes require 72-hour advance notice to prevent disruptions, (2) clients need a documented escalation path for support, and (3) rate limit headers must be included in all API responses to help clients monitor their usage proactively. These lessons should inform the new webhooks feature design by ensuring notification mechanisms, clear communication protocols, and transparent rate limit visibility are built in from the start.",
